    The algebra $\kbb Q/J$ is a string algebra.
    By identifying the vertices of $Q$ with the elements of $\Zbb^2$, we get an equivalence of categories
    $\rep(Q,I) \simeq \rep(\Zbb^2)$.

    Note that $I \subseteq J$, which induces a fully faithful functor $F : \rep(Q,J) \to \rep(Q,I) \simeq \rep(\Zbb^2)$,
    and that $M \in \rep(\Zbb^2)$ is in the essential image of $F$ if and only if $M$ is ephemeral, since the ideal~$J$ consists of all paths in $Q$ that strictly increase both coordinates.
