    Then $\partial \kbb_I \cong \kbb_{\gamma, \Tcal}$, where $\Tcal$ is the $1\times 1$ identity matrix.
    The result then follows by additivity and the uniqueness of decompositions into boundary component representations (\cref{theorem:boundary-tame}).
