\subsection{Planar limit of rungs, braids, caps, and cups}

In the planar limit, the fundamental rungs attached to heavy strands obey a specific set of relations. Here we give a three-dimensional "geometric" picture of those relations, which we use to manipulate the rungs and compute the augmentation variety. It is understood that the $\olambda_i$ and $\omu_i$ in the formulae correspond to components of heavy strands in a knot/link.

To avoid labeling every heavy strand with its representation, we can consider knots with a \textit{basepoint}. Keeping track of the labeling is equivalent to the following relations involving the basepoint:
\begin{align}
