For the unknot we can start with $f^u_1=-\omu (g\olambda^{-1}-g^{-1}\olambda)$, braid it to obtain $f^a_{+;1,4}=-f^a_2$, and braid it back to $-g\olambda^{-2}e^u_3=g\olambda^{-2}(\olambda-\olambda^{-1})$. This gives the augmentation variety of the unknot, accounting for the framing.

For the left-handed trefoil we can start with the rungs $f^u_1$, $f^u_{-;1,3}$ and $f^u_{-;1,4}$, and perform the usual manipulations to obtain relations
\begin{align}
    -\omu (g^2-\olambda^2)&=g\olambda f^a_2 (\olambda^2-2+ge^a_2f^a_2)\cr
   \omu\olambda e^a_2 &= \olambda^2-1+g e^a_2 f^a_2\cr
    g\omu e^a_2&=-\olambda^2f^a_2 \, ,
\end{align}
and obtain the augmentation variety
\begin{equation}
    0 = g^6 \omu -2 g^4 \olambda ^4 \omu -g^4 \olambda ^2 \omu -g^4 \olambda ^2+g^4+g^2 \olambda ^8 \omu -g^2 \olambda ^6 \omu ^2-g^2 \olambda ^6 \omu
   +2 g^2 \olambda ^4 \omu +\olambda ^8 \omu ^2\, ,
\end{equation}
which is mapped to the usual right-handed trefoil augmentation variety by the chirality reversal map $\omu\to \omu^{-1}$, $\olambda \to \olambda g^{-1}$, $g\to g^{-1}$.

