%
\caption{$1/|H_\rho^{(2)}(\alpha)|^2$ .vs. the complex energy $E$ with $\alpha=3.14$ and $m_\sigma=440$ MeV in the $\Sigma_c^+ \bar{D}^{0}$ case. The pole of $1/|H_\rho^{(2)}(\alpha)|^2$ corresponds to a zero point of the second kind of Hankel function $H_\rho^{(2)}(\alpha)$, which represents a resonance state of $\Sigma_c^+ \bar{D}^{0}$, as labeled in the figure.}
