\begin{abstract}
 In this paper, we present \MyMthd{}, a training-free token compression strategy designed for video multimodal large language models. Previous methods mostly attempt to compress tokens based on attention scores, but fail to effectively capture all semantic regions and often lead to token redundancy. Differently, we propose to leverage the Semantic Connected Components (SCC) approach that assigns
 % a single token to each distinct semantic region 
tokens to distinct semantic regions
 within the token set, ensuring comprehensive semantic coverage. The outcome is a two-step spatio-temporal token compression strategy that utilizes SCC in both spatial and temporal domains. This strategy can effectively compress tokens by representing the entire video with a set of non-overlapping semantic tokens. 
 We conduct extensive evaluations of the token compression capabilities of \MyMthd{} across diverse video understanding benchmarks, including video question answering, long video understanding, and comprehensive multi-choices benchmarks.
 Experimental results show that the proposed \MyMthd{} outperforms other token compression methods, achieving superior performance in various video understanding benchmarks, particularly at low token retention ratios. 

 Project page: \url{https://github.com/HumanMLLM/LLaVA-Scissor}.
 % Our code will be made open-sourced.
\end{abstract}


\section{Introduction}
% Video Multimodal Large Language Models 
Recently, Video Large Language Models (VLLMs)~\cite{li2023videochat,maaz2023video,lin2023video,wang2024internvideo2,liu2024world, zhao2025facial, achiam2023gpt, zhao2025humanomni} have achieved remarkable progress due to the rapid advancement of Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs)~\cite{Qwen2-VL, li2024llava, chen2023internvl, gpt4v, zhu2023minigpt,chen2024expanding,ye2023mplugowl,bai2023qwen,dong2024internlm}.
% as video is the most prevalent form of real-world interaction. 
% Among them, the video modality, as the most prevalent form of real-world interaction, has attracted particular attention.
%一个典型的MLLM通常由一个visual encoder，一个visual projector和一个large language model组成。在面对视频输入时，与处理单张图像类似，先用视觉编码器处理和提取每一帧的特征；再用视觉投影器将视觉特征映射到可以与文本特征有效结合的空间，即形成LLM可以理解的visual tokens，最后与用户instructions一起送入LLM decoder，基于结合后的视觉和文本表示生成连贯且上下文相关的文本。
% A typical VLLMs~\cite{li2023videochat,maaz2023video,lin2023video,wang2024internvideo2,liu2024world, zhao2025facial, achiam2023gpt} consists of a visual encoder to extract embeddings from video frames, a visual projector to map visual embedding into video tokens, and a LLM decoder to generate the response based on the integrated text instructions and video tokens. 
% The visual encoder extracts features from each video frame, which are then mapped into video tokens by the visual projector. These tokens, along with user instructions, are input into the LLM decoder to generate the response based on the integrated representations.
% 然而，与处理单张图像不同，由于video MLLM需要对序列化的每一帧视频数据进行独立编码，这导致即使从视频中采样出少量帧，就会产生非常多的video token，以LLaVA-OneVision举例，32 frames 就对应 6272 token。于此同时，由于attention机制导致运算的复杂度随着token数量的增加以平方级上升，显著增加了视频MLLM的训练和推理的成本。
% However, 
Unlike processing a single image, VLLMs often require independent encoding of each video frame in a serialized sequence. As a result, even when only a small number of frames are sampled from a video, a large number of visual tokens are generated. 
% For example, in LLaVA-OneVision~\cite{li2024llavaone}, 32 frames correspond to 6272 tokens.
% Additionally, due to the attention mechanism in LLMs, the computational complexity increases quadratically with the number of tokens, significantly increasing the training and inference costs for video MLLMs.
% 尽管有些方法从网络结构或者trainable 模块的角度尝试减少视觉token的数量，然而，这些方法不仅需要额外的training 成本，其专门设计的结构与现有通用MLLdM的不兼容也限制了其可移植性。因此，training-free 的作用在inference阶段的token reduction方案are necessary。
Although some methods attempt to reduce the number of visual tokens from the perspective of network architecture~\cite{li2024llamavid, xue2024xgenmmblip3familyopen, ye2024voco} or trainable modules~\cite{blip3video-xgenmmvid, zhang2023vision, allakhverdov2025enoughadaptivetokenreduction}, these approaches not only involve additional training costs but also face limitations in portability due to their specialized structures. Therefore, training-free token reduction strategies during the inference phase are essential for more efficient and scalable video processing.

% 从所有token中选出最有代表性的token是常见的token reduction方案。之前的用于image token 压缩的方案，大多从attention score的角度出发，尝试选出最重要的token，然而，用这样的方法选出的token过于强调关键对象，并不能覆盖token中的全部语义，也会导致关键语义被多次选择。
Selecting the most representative tokens~\cite{fayyaz2022ats, shen2024tempme, bolya2022tome} from all tokens is one of the most common paradigms for token reduction. Previous methods designed for image token compression~\cite{yang2024visionzip, shang2024LLaVAPruMerge} often focus on leveraging attention scores to identify the most important tokens. However, as shown in \figref{fig: pattern}(a), attention-based approaches~\cite{chen2024image, zhang2024sparsevlm, xing2024pyramiddrop, liu2024multi} tend to prioritize only key objects, which can result in an incomplete representation of all semantics and the repeated selection of key semantics at the same time.
% Therefore, 为了尽可能找出所有不重叠的语义区域来代表整段视频，我们提出了一种通过查找语义相同的连通分量的方法，termed SCC。通过度量token之间pairwise相似度，SCC能够将给定token划分为不重叠的区域，并将每个独立的语义区域用一个单独的token来表示，极大。值得一提的是，由于SCC并不要求token在位置上相邻，
Therefore, to identify all distinct semantic regions that can effectively represent the entire video with less redundancy, we propose the Semantic Connected Components (SCC) strategy. By measuring pairwise similarity between tokens, SCC can partition the tokens into non-overlapping regions throughout identifying connected components, and 
% use a single token to represent each distinct semantic region. 
use tokens to represent distinct semantic regions. 
% This significantly enhances the efficiency of token selection. 
Notably, SCC does not require the tokens to be positional adjacent, allowing it to capture global semantic relations throughout the entire token sequence, regardless of spatial positioning. This enables a more comprehensive and efficient representation of video content.

% Also，考虑到基于image的方案都无法考虑视频帧在时序上存在的冗余,一些方法开始尝试专门为video设计压缩方案。然而，这些方法往往关注如何对video划分segment并apply inter-segment token compression，或者在时序上对锚定固定像素位置token进行压缩，然而，这些方法忽略了一个事实，语义相同的区域并不一定在时序上相连，也不一定在时序上保持空间位置的不变,这为他们的方案带来了潜在的冗余。
%因此，Equipped with the SCC，我们提出了一种two-step spatio-temperal token compression策略。具体来说，我们首先为每一个视频帧找到其空间位置上的所有独特语义区域，再从时序上考虑这些语义区域之间的相似性并进行进一步压缩，最终使用一组不包含重复语义语义的token表示整段video。
Considering that image-based methods fail to account for the temporal redundancy across video frames, some approaches~\cite{tao2024dycoke, huang2024prunevid, liu2025hybrid} begin to design compression strategies specifically for videos. 
% However, these methods often focus on how to segment the video and compress tokens based on fixed pixel positions in the temporal domain. They overlook a crucial fact: semantically similar regions are not necessarily spatially connected, nor do they necessarily maintain their spatial positions over time.
As shown in \figref{fig: pattern}(b), these methods often focus on segmenting the video and applying inter-segment token compression~\cite{shen2025fastvid, guo2025fila, videollamb}, or compressing tokens based on fixed pixel positions across time~\cite{shen2024longvu}. However, they overlook the fact that semantically similar regions may not be temporally connected or maintain spatial consistency over time, which introduces potential redundancy.
To tackle this, we introduce \MyMthd{}, a two-step spatio-temporal token compression strategy as shown in \figref{fig: pattern}(c) with the help of SCC. Specifically, we first identify all unique semantic regions within the spatial domain of each video frame. Then, we assess the SCC again to remove temporal redundancy over semantic regions across frames and perform a further fusion. The result is a set of tokens that can effectively represent the entire video, without redundancy, and with each token encapsulating distinct semantic information from both spatial and temporal perspectives.

% 使用an enhanced LLaVA-OneVision 模型作为基础模型，我们在三个video question answering benchmark，四个Long Video understanding benchmark，以及多选benchmark MVBench上验证了我们的方法。结果说明我们的方法一致性的优于其他方法，尤其是在token 保留率较低的时候。
We evaluate our \MyMthd{} on three video question answering benchmarks, four long video understanding benchmarks, and the multi-choice benchmark MVBench leveraging an enhanced LLaVA-OneVision model as the base model. The results demonstrate that our method consistently outperforms other token compression approaches, particularly at lower token retention ratios.
% 最后，我们还尝试分析了reducing law in video token compression。通过分析随着token保留率降低，现有token压缩方法在various benchmark上的性能变化，说明在相对较高的保留率下，各个方法的性能与原始模型性能差距很小，这说明video token存在明确的冗余，在保留token数量较少时，由于关键语义信息被损坏，性能开始出现快速下降，我们的方法比起其他方法更能保留关键的语义信息。
Finally, we analyze the reducing law in video token compression in \secref{sec: reducing law} by evaluating performance changes across benchmarks as the token retention ratio decreases. The results demonstrate that the redundancy of video tokens indeed exists, and our method, compared to others, is more effective in preserving key semantics at lower retention ratios, leading to superior performance.
%All methods perform comparable performance to the original model at relative higher retention ratios, indicating significant redundancy in video tokens. And as the retention ratio drops, performance declines rapidly due to the loss of key semantic information. our \MyMthd{} still outperforms others in retaining critical semantics, even with fewer tokens.

Our contributions can be summarized as follows:
\begin{itemize}
% We point out 现有的基于attention score选择重要token的方式不能完整的代表整个token set and 提出了Semantic Connected Components (SCC), 一种通过查找token set中全部独特语义区域的token压缩策略。
    \item We point out that existing attention score-based methods
    % , which only select important tokens, 
    fail to fully represent the entire token set and propose Semantic Connected Components (SCC), a token compression strategy that captures all distinct semantic regions within the token set.
    \item We propose \MyMthd{}, a two-step spatio-temporal token compression designed for video MLLMs, which can generate a more comprehensive and efficient representation of video content. Experiments show that \MyMthd{} outperforms other token compression methods on various video understanding benchmarks.
    % \item We analyze the reducing law in video token compression to highlight the redundancy in video tokens and show \MyMthd{} can preserve key semantic information at low retention ratios.
\end{itemize}

