\section{Related Work}
\subsection{Video Large Language Models}
Benefiting from the rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs)~\cite{brown2020language,ouyang2022training,chatgpt,vicuna2023,touvron2023llama2,jiang2024mixtral,guo2025deepseek,liu2024deepseek,qwen2.5}, a wide range of powerful proprietary MLLMs~\cite{gpt4v, openai2023gpt4, Claude2024, geminiteam2024geminifamilyhighlycapable, openai2024gpt4o} and open-source community MLLMs~\cite{liu2024visual, liu2023llava, liu2023llava1.5, zhang2024llavanext-video,li2024llavanext-ablations, ye2023mplug, ye2023mplugowl2, gao2023llama} have emerged. 
%
Among them, Video Large Language Models (VLLMs)~\cite{zhao2025llava, zhao2025r1, zhang2024llavanextvideo} tailored for video understanding have gained increasing attention.
Typical VLLMs~\cite{lin2023video, damonlpsg2023videollama, Maaz2023VideoChatGPT} encode video frame sequences into raw video tokens with visual encoder and projector, and then 
feed them into LLMs along with user instructions to generate responses.
% utilize LLMs to generate responses along with user instructions.
% 典型的VLLMs 直接将video 帧序列编码为 raw video tokens, the constraint on context length inevitably causes a trade-off between the number of tokens per frame and the number of frames to input. VideoChat and Video-LLaVA
Methods such as MovieChat~\cite{song2023moviechat}, TimeChat~\cite{Ren2023TimeChat} and TimeSuite~\cite{ zeng2024timesuite} develop memory modules and timestamp-aware encoders 
% to model fine-grained temporal information
for capturing better context.
% To 更好的理解视频上下文，some approaches develop memory modules and timestamp-aware encoders to capture detailed video content.
% Methods like Oryx, LLaVA-Video 通过拓展大量数据，极大提升了模型基准。
% 一些方法直接使用了video encoder以获取更多的综合时空信息。
LLaVA-OneVision~\cite{li2024llavaone} proposes a unified model capable of handling images, videos, audios, and other modalities simultaneously.
LLaVA-Next-Video~\cite{zhang2024videoinstructiontuningsynthetic} significantly improves model performance by leveraging large-scale synthetic data.
% 然而，由于要对帧序列进行逐个编码，token数量的快速增加导致现有VLLMs在长视频理解和效率上面临挑战，这使得减少token数量尤其重要。
However, since the sequential encoding of frames leads to an increase in token numbers, existing VLLMs struggle in processing long video and computational efficiency, emphasizing the necessity of token reduction.

\subsection{Token Reduction in MLLMs}
Token reduction~\cite{bolya2022tome, rao2021dynamicvit, koner2024lookupvit, liang2022not} is essential for efficient inference and longer visual sequences, and has been extended to the MLLMs domain~\cite{ye2024mplugowl3longimagesequenceunderstanding, shi2023crossget, han2025filtercorrelatecompresstrainingfree, chen2024efficient, TokenPacker}. Approaches such as LLaMA-VID~\cite{li2024llamavid} and LongVA~\cite{zhang2024longcontexttransferlanguage} design token-efficient architectures, while other methods like LongVU~\cite{shen2024longvu}, VideoLLaMA~\cite{damonlpsg2024videollama2, damonlpsg2025videollama3}, and VideoLLaMB~\cite{videollamb}  reduce token numbers through projector-level modifications. 
Pooling-based approaches~\cite{xu2024pllava, yao2024deco, weng2024longvlmefficientlongvideo} are also widely used.
Additionally, some methods~\cite{wang2024lifelongmemoryleveragingllmsanswering, zhang2023simple, wang2024videoagentlongformvideounderstanding} explore agent-based techniques to convert videos into textual descriptions.

As for training-free strategies, the most common approach is to select the important tokens from the token set~\cite{shang2024LLaVAPruMerge, yang2025topv, wang2025dymudynamicmergingvirtual, Ye2024ATPLLaVAAT}. 
% VisionZip根据attention socre选取domaint tokens
Some methods leverage the attention score of [CLS] token~\cite{yang2024visionzip, zhang2024fastervlm, zhang2024token, wang2024cls} to measure the importance of each token.
FastV~\cite{chen2024image} proposes a strategy to select key tokens during the prefilling stage based on attention maps, while VTW~\cite{lin2024boosting} introduces an aggressive approach that directly removes visual tokens after a certain decoder layer.
% FastV提供了一种在prefilling阶段依据attention map选取关键token的策略，VTW则是提出了一种在decoder指定层后直接去除visual tokens的激进策略。
% Some method lervage [CLS] token~\cite{visionzip, zhang2024fastervlm, zhang2024token} 来衡量token的重要性。
However, these image token compression methods overlook the temporal redundancy across video frames. 
DyCoke~\cite{tao2024dycoke} uniformly divides videos into segments and performs intra-segment compression by fixed even-odd token grouping. PruneVID~\cite{huang2024prunevid} and FastVID~\cite{shen2025fastvid} first segment the video based on scene boundaries and cluster video tokens within each segment. However, these segment-based methods overlook the fact that semantically similar information may not be temporally adjacent or spatially consistent, leading to redundancy when stacking tokens from each segment, as shown in \figref{fig: pattern}(b).
% DyCoke将视频均匀划分为segment，对token进行固定的奇偶分组进行segment内的压缩。
% PruneVID and FastVID则是先根据场景划分segment，再在segment内进行video tokens的聚类。
% 这些划分segment的方法忽略了相同语义信息并不一定在时序上相邻或者在空间上不变，因此在堆叠每个segment压缩后的token时，仍然会产生冗余。之前的方法大都局限于在某一帧或图像内或者某一空间位置的不同时序进行token压缩
% Different from them, \MyMthd{} 在空间和时序上同时进行了token压缩，用一组语义不重叠的video token代表整个video。
Different from them, \MyMthd{} performs token compression across both spatial and temporal dimensions, representing the entire video with a set of semantically non-overlapping video tokens.



\section{\MyMthd{}}
% \subsection{Preliminary}

% 我们的方法包括两个部分，首先，我们提出了一种利用连通图寻找给定token中所有独特语义区域并将其合并的方法。之后，在此基础上，我们进一步提出了一种在空序和时序上两次使用该方法进行token合并的方案。
In this section, we first propose the Semantic Connected Components (SCC) approach to identify distinct semantic regions within a given token set by utilizing connected components. Then, we propose a two-step scheme that applies the SCC strategy in spatial and temporal domains to achieve effective token compression for video understanding.

\subsection{Token Compression via Semantic Connected Components (SCC)}

\label{sec: Connected Components}
% 我们的semantic connected components token merge 策略可以被描述为
% Previous methods based on similarity have demonstrated that tokens with high similarity often encapsulate analogous semantics, suggesting the potential for further fusion.  However, when dealing with the situation of selecting retained tokens for merging, whether through pre-sampling or importance-based selection, these approaches can potentially result in the selection of redundant semantic regions or the omission of certain semantic regions.
As shown in \figref{fig: pattern}(a), prior attention-based token selection approaches tend to select redundant semantic regions while overlooking others, making it challenging to obtain a representative and comprehensive token set.
% methods based on similarity have demonstrated that tokens with high similarity indicate similar semantics, suggesting the potential for further fusion. 
% However, determining which tokens should be retained for merging is a challenging task. Whether through pre-sampling or importance-based selection, these approaches may inadvertently select redundant semantic regions or overlook certain semantic areas.
%之前的很多基于相似度的方法已经证明，相似度高的token表明其包含了相似的语义，因此可以对其进行融合。然而，选择保留哪些token接收合并是一个有挑战性的任务，不管是提前采样，还是根据基于重要性的选择，这些方案既有可能选择到重复的语义区域，也有可能导致一些语义区域被忽略。
Different from them, we tend to identify all unique semantic regions and retain one single token for each distinct region. 

Given a set of tokens $ \mathbf{K} = \{\mathbf{k}_1, ..., \mathbf{k}_{\mathbf{N}}\}\in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbf{N}\times d}$, we first compute the pairwise similarity between each token and then convert it into a binary map $\mathcal{A}$ based on a threshold $\tau$, as shown in \eqnref{eqn: adjacency matrix}:
% 假设给定一组token K\in \mathbb{R}^{N\times c},我们首先计算token两两之间的相似度,并根据阈值$\tau$将其转换为二元map A.
\begin{equation} 
\label{eqn: adjacency matrix}
    \mathcal{A} = (\frac{\mathbf{K}\cdot \mathbf{K}^T}{||\mathbf{K}||_{dim=1}\cdot||\mathbf{K}||_{dim=1}} > \tau)
    \in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbf{N}\times \mathbf{N}}.
\end{equation}

In the binary similarity map $\mathcal{A}$, $\mathcal{A}(i, j)$ indicates the similarity between any two tokens $ \mathbf{k}_i$ and $ \mathbf{k}_j$. Therefore, if we consider each token as a vertex and treat $\mathcal{A}$ as an adjacency matrix representing the connectivity between vertices, we can construct a graph based on the similarity relationships inherent in $\mathcal{A}$. 
% Consequently, in order to identify all distinct semantic regions, we transform the problem of finding all unique semantic regions into the task of identifying all connected components in the graph using the adjacency matrix $\mathcal{A}$.
In this case, the problem of finding all unique semantic regions can be transformed into the task of identifying all connected components in the graph using the adjacency matrix $\mathcal{A}$.
% 在这个二元相似度map A 中，A(i,j) 标记了任意两个token k_i, k_j 之间的相似性，因此，如果我们将每一个token视为一个节点，将A视为标记节点间连通性的邻接矩阵，那么我们便可以利用A中蕴含的相似关系建立一个graph。因此，为了尽可能找到全部的独特的语义区域，我们将寻找所有独特语义区域的问题转换为根据邻接矩阵A寻找图中全部连通分量。

To tackle this, we present an approximate method for computing the connected components.
% (detailed in supplementary materials \secref{sec: approximate components}). 
Specifically, given the adjacency matrix $\mathcal{A}$, we first sample a subset of vertices from the $N$ vertices based on an error tolerance $\epsilon$. The number of vertices sampled is determined as follows:
% In \algref{alg:approximate_components} 中，我们给出了一种近似求解连通分量的方案。具体来说，给定邻接矩阵A，我们首先从$N$个节点中根据error tolerance e 采样出一些节点，采样数量为：
\begin{equation}
\label{eqn: sample}
    \mathbf{N}' = \min(\mathbf{N}, \lceil \frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^2}\rceil).
\end{equation}
%.之后，我们使用带有路径压缩和按秩合并的并查集查集查找图中的连通分量，将连通分量集合记作$C = \{C_1, ..., C_M\}$. Note that in case 当前连通分量无法覆盖全部的token，每一个未被覆盖到的token都被视为一个单独的连通分量。同时，为了尽量不破坏token之间的相对位置关系，我们对连通分量按照每个cluster中度数最高的节点标号对其进行了排序，最终得到所有token的语义连通分量$C = \{C_1, ..., C_M\}$，其中$|C| = M$，表示共有M个连通分量。这suggest在包含N个token的K中，存在M个独特的语义区域。
% 对于N'中的每一个节点，我们根据邻接矩阵找到其所有的邻居创建邻接表。
For each sampled vertex, we 
identify all its neighbors based on the adjacency matrix $\mathcal{A}$ and 
% create a adjacency list. Then, we 
employ the union-find data structure with path compression and union-by-rank
% based on $\mathcal{A}$
% (detailed in supplementary materials \secref{sec: unionfind})
to identify all connected components in the graph. Note that when the connected components extracted from $\mathbf{N'}$ sampled vertex do not cover all $\mathbf{N}$ vertices, each uncovered vertex would be viewed as a separate connected component. Additionally, to preserve the relative positional relationships among tokens, we sort the connected components based on the vertex ID with the highest degree within each cluster. Detailed data structure and approximate connected components algorithm are detailed in \secref{sec: algorithms} of appendix.

The sorted connected components set is denoted as  $C = \{C_1, ..., C_M\}$, where $M$ indicates there are totally $M$ connected components in the graph, and
each $C_i$ in $ C $ consists of $|C_i|$ unique vertices.
% , as shown in \eqnref{each connected component}.
% \begin{equation}
% \label{each connected component}
%     C_i = \{\mathbf{k}_{{i_1}}, \mathbf{k}{_{i_2}}, ... , \mathbf{k}_{i_{|C_i|}}\}
% \end{equation}
%同时，连通分量能够将有N个节点的图划分为M个不相交的子图，任意两个连通分量之间没有交集，所有连通分量的节点数之等于图的节点数。
As expressed in \eqnref{property}, since connected components can partition a graph with N vertices into M disjoint subgraphs, no two connected components intersect, and the total number of vertices across all connected components equals the number of vertices in the graph.
\begin{equation}
\label{property}
   \forall i,j \in [1, M], C_i \cap C_j = \varnothing ; \sum^{M}_{i=1}|C_i| = \mathbf{N}.
\end{equation}
% 这一性质 suggests that token集合K可以根据语义相似度被划分为M个distinct semantic regions。
This property suggests that the token set $\mathbf{K}$ can be partitioned into $M$ distinct semantic regions throughout connected components $C$, which can encompass all non-overlapping semantics indicated by similarity map $\mathcal{A}$.
% 最后，我们依据$C$对全部token K进行合并，对于C中的每一个连通分量$C_i$，$|C_i|$表示第 i 个连通分量中节点的数量，我们将其合并为一个token，进而将N个token的K压缩为仅有M个token的K'
% Therefore, we can compress the token set $\mathbf{K}$ based on connected components $C$. To avoid redundancy, 
% for each connected component $C_i$ in $C$, where $|C_i|$ represents the number of vertices in the $i$-th connected component, 
% we aggregate the tokens within each $C_i$ in $C$ into a single token, detailed in \eqnref{eqn: merge}.
% 考虑到使用带有路径压缩和按秩合并的并查集查找图中连通分量的时间复杂度为O(N + M\alpha)，其中m为图中的边数，\alpha (\cdot)为阿克曼函数的反函数（一般情况下可视为小于5的常数），M的取值最大为 $N * N'$，因此，该算法的复杂度为$O(N*log(N)\alpha(M+N, N))$
Therefore, we can compress the token set $\mathbf{K}$ into $\mathbf{K}'$ by aggregating the tokens within each $C_i$ in $C$ 
% into a single token 
to avoid redundancy, detailed in \eqnref{eqn: merge}:
\begin{equation}
\label{eqn: merge}
     \mathbf{k}'_i = \frac{1}{|C_i|}\sum^{|C_i|}_{j=1}{\mathbf{k}_{i_j}}, i = 1, ..., M; \mathbf{K'} = \text{concat}[\mathbf{k}'_1, ... ,\mathbf{k}'_M] .
\end{equation}
% This process reduces the original token set $K \in \mathbb{R}^{N\times c}$ into $K' \in \mathbb{R}^{M\times c}$.
This process constructs a representative token for each unique semantic region, thus transforming the original token set $ \mathbf{K} \in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbf{N}\times c} $ into $ \mathbf{K}' \in \mathbb{R}^{M\times c} $. 
Leveraging this characteristic, we are able to get representative tokens from a token set, regardless of their positional adjacency. 
% Also, since every $ \mathbf{k}' $ in $ \mathbf{K}' $ can represent an independent and unique semantic region, we treat them as the retained tokens for further token merging.
% This process为每一个unique 语义region 构造了一个代表它的token，thus turn the original token set $K \in \mathbb{R}^{N\times c}$ into $K' \in \mathbb{R}^{M\times c}$. Since every k' in K' 都能代表一个独立的不重复的语义区域，我们可以将其视为retained tokens for token merge.


