We observe in Figure \ref {TSUS_2_1} that maximum fairness can be reached when the \mbox{Wi-Fi} uses A-MPDU-based frame aggregation. On the other hand, when \mbox{Wi-Fi} APs do not opt for frame aggregation, the value of the fairness index decreases due to shorter \mbox{Wi-Fi} transmission time in comparison to \mbox{NR-U} MCOT duration.       
