The third challenge is to design an efficient audit mechanism for \data's untrusted inference software that achieves both high efficiency and scalability.
This is especially critical during peak inference stages characterized by large query volumes and stringent low-latency demands.
The inherent performance disparity, where the TEE-COO trusted path is considerably slower than \data's native software execution on untrusted GPU~\cite{LiZGC0ZG21,LeeLPLLLXXZS19}, means that a naive approach of auditing every inference instance would introduce unacceptable system overhead and degrade service throughput.
