\subsection{Motivation Scenario.}
\label{subsec:motivation_scenario}
Consider a VFL system deployed in the FinTech domain for applications like joint credit risk assessment~\cite{wu2023bloomberggpt,XingCHLZ24}.
In such a distributed software system,  digital bank \task collaborates with a mobile payment platform \data (e.g., Alipay or PayPal) to compute credit scores, leveraging their respective private datasets--\task's loan application and repayment histories, and \data's rich transactional and behavioral data for the same users.
\coord is usually a regulatory body that is recognized by multiple parties and able to remain neutral, assisting in auditing while helping to aggregate representations~\cite{JiangZG22a,LiuFCXY21}.
% \chongru{citations}
The system must support high-throughput, low-latency inference during peak events (e.g., Singles Day, Cyber Monday, month-end paydays)~\cite{SoiferLLZLHZOMB19,GujaratiKAHKVM20}.
Ensuring \data’s inference software executes correctly under these stresses is critical, as errors could produce faulty scores and incur substantial financial losses for \task.
