\myparagraph{Remark.}
Most of the defense mechanisms against poisoning attacks on FL are designed for HFL~\cite{SandeepaSWL24,KabirSRM24,MozaffariSH23,FereidooniPRDS24,ChuGISL23,ShejwalkarH21,KraussD23}.
Since the training paradigms and architectures of VFL and HFL are significantly different, the defense mechanisms in HFL cannot be applied to VFL~\cite{BaiCZ0WG23,naseri2023badvfl}.

\subsection{TEE-COO Framework}
\label{subsec:tee_coo}
% \myparagraph{Characteristic.}
% The TEE-COO framework has been widely applied in FL~\cite{MoHKMPK21,Kato0Y23}.
% We leverage the TEE-COO collaborative inference mechanism in VFL to assist \task in auditing the inferences of \data.
The TEE-COO framework is widely adopted in FL~\cite{MoHKMPK21,Kato0Y23} and multi-party ML systems~\cite{abs-1912-03485,mo2020darknetz,Zhangteeslice2024}.
We leverage the TEE-COO collaborative inference in VFL to assist \task in auditing the execution of \data's untrusted inference software.
% This mechanism is a widely used framework for securing inference in the multi-party ML system~\cite{abs-1912-03485,mo2020darknetz,Zhangteeslice2024}.
It can be viewed as an extension of edge-cloud collaborative inference, where the edge (\data) is equipped with a TEE, and the cloud serves as \coord.
The service provider can run the validation programs in the TEE to ensure the trustworthiness of the inference results.
TEE creates isolated secure enclaves, protecting computations from the untrusted edge environment, but typically offers limited computational resources and may be 6-7$\times$ slower compared to native inference software execution~\cite{LiZGC0ZG21,LeeLPLLLXXZS19}.
% The characteristic of TEE is its ability to isolate a secure enclave from the edge environment, ensuring that computations within the enclave are protected from manipulation by the untrusted edge.
% But it has limited computational resources and comparatively low inference (sometimes the
% performance overhead is 6-7$\times$ slower than the native inference)~\cite{LiZGC0ZG21,LeeLPLLLXXZS19}.
Conversely, \coord provides substantial computational resources but might not be fully trusted by \data, making it suitable for processing computation-intensive yet less privacy-sensitive model segments~\cite{abs-1912-03485,mo2020darknetz}.
% The characteristic of \coord is that it has high computational resources but may
% not be fully trusted by \data.
% Thus it is suitable for running the computation-intensive but non-sensitive part of the inference program~\cite{abs-1912-03485,mo2020darknetz}.
\data partitions its bottom model $f_d$ into a shallow, privacy-sensitive part $f_d^{sm}$ processed within its local TEE, and a deeper, more computationally intensive part $f_d^{dm}$ offloaded to \coord (as depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:model_partition}).
