\myparagraph{Advantages.}
TEE-COO has several advantages over prior frameworks. 
Compared with the edge-cloud framework, TEE-COO can defend against the attack from edge owners or third-party attackers on the edge~\cite{sun2023shadownet,Zhangteeslice2024} by running validation programs in the TEE.
Compared with the TEE-only framework, TEE-COO can reduce the computation overhead of the TEE by offloading the computation-intensive part to \coord~\cite{abs-1912-03485,ShenQJWWCZWCLZC22,TramerB19}. 
Compared with the \coord-only framework, TEE-COO can protect data privacy by running the inference program on the edge to comply with the privacy protection of VFL.

\myparagraph{SGX.}
The implementation of our work is based on Intel SGX~\footnote{\method's implementation does not depend on a specific TEE instance (discussed in Sec.~\ref{sec:discussion})} due to its mature status and wide availability on commercial platforms, such as IBM, Microsoft, and Alibaba cloud servers~\cite{sgx_available_blog}, aligning with prior research highlighting its accessibility~\cite{mo2020darknetz,Zhangteeslice2024}.
Given that VFL participants are often organizations with adequate computing infrastructure, a SGX-based solution is considered practical and feasible~\cite{YangLCT19,LiuKZPHYOZY24}.

