\myparagraph{TEE Security.}
We assume TEE is available on \data's machine following prior work~\cite{Zhang0ZZZ0W24,Zhangteeslice2024}.
\task utilizes the TEE on \data's machine to audit the \data's inference.
We follow prior work to adopt three security features provided by SGX: remote attestation, encryption, and integrity~\cite{sun2023shadownet,Zhangteeslice2024}.
Remote attestation enables \task to verify and securely execute a trusted program within the TEE enclave.
Encryption ensures that the runtime data is encrypted, and \data cannot see the data
in TEE.
Integrity ensures that the external untrusted environment cannot affect the operation of programs in TEE.
Additionally, TEE can encrypt data and store the encrypted data on disk.
To prevent data inconsistency, every time TEE loads encrypted data, it checks the integrity.
Besides, we do not consider the security issues of compromising TEE confidentiality from side channels, which is consistent with previous work~\cite{mo2020darknetz,Zhangteeslice2024}.
