\myparagraph{Coordinator.}
\coord provides high-performance computing resources and is assumed to follow the \textit{semi-honest} model, as in prior work~\cite{HeZL19,YangLCT19}.
Specifically, \coord honestly executes the required computation tasks without modifying the data or model during training and inference.
In \train, \coord is used only as an aggregator, but acts as both an aggregator and performs outsourced inference in \infer, allowing it to leverage additional knowledge to infer \data's private data.
\coord, as an independent third party, will not collude with \task and \data following prior work~\cite{YangLCT19,XuB00JL21}.
In FinTech scenarios, \coord is usually a regulatory body recognized by multiple parties and able to remain neutral~\cite{JiangZG22a,LiuFCXY21}.
