where $b\le |B|, o\le |O|$, $T_o$ denotes the execution time of operation $o$, and $\beta_{o,b}^{end}$ is the completion time of operation $o$ in block $b$.
The optimization seeks the number of blocks $B_*$ that minimizes the total inference latency without violating memory or concurrency constraints.
Eq.~\ref{eq:epc} ensures that the size of the block and $f_d^{sm}$ does not exceed the EPC size.
Eq.~\ref{eq:order} ensures that each block executes all operations sequentially.
Eq.~\ref{eq:resource} stipulates that a given resource can be allocated to only one block at any given time.
