\myparagraph{Implementation Considerations.}
In practice, \method uses runtime profiling during the initial model validation phase to estimate operation-wise latencies $T_{tee}, T_{comm}, T_{coo}$.
The communication time $T_{comm}$ is treated as a constant due to its relatively stable behavior across blocks~\cite{Jiang0C24}.
These statistics are then used to determine the optimal block configuration $B^{*}$ through limited enumeration, avoiding runtime complexity.

