\noindent \textbf{\ding{175} Inference Consistency Validation.}
The auditing engine at \task compares the outputs from both inference pipelines: untrusted vs. trusted.
Any inconsistency is flagged as a violation of execution integrity.
This dual-execution strategy, inspired by N-version programming~\cite{chen1978n,avizienis1995methodology}, enables robust detection without interrupting normal inference flow or incurring additional latency.
By embedding runtime validation into the system architecture, \method transforms inference integrity from a post hoc concern into an auditable, real-time software property.
