\subsubsection{Case 2: $\eta = 0$}


In the case when $\eta = 0$, where execution costs are purely linear ($L(v) = \frac{\psi}{2} |v|$), there is no closed-form solution, so we rely on a comparison between the RL policy and the policy derived from the numerical solution of the HJB equation. Figure~\ref{fig:RL_eta_0_actions} shows the policies corresponding to the two numerical methods. \\

