\subsection{Dataset} 
\label{subsec:dataset}
The study utilizes an augmented version of the \textit{Predict Students' Dropout and Academic Success} dataset \cite{cortez2022predict}, originally sourced from the UCI Machine Learning Repository (\url{https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/697/predict+students+dropout+and+academic+success}). This longitudinal dataset tracks Portuguese higher education students across multiple academic terms. 

\textbf{Original Structure:} The dataset contains 4,423 de-identified student records with 36 features spanning:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*,noitemsep]
    \item \textbf{Socio-demographic status}: 29 integer variables (e.g., scholarship holder, debtor status)
    \item \textbf{Academic performance}: 5 floating-point metrics (e.g., curricular unit grades, enrollment age)
    \item \textbf{Macro-indicators}: National GDP during enrollment year
    \item \textbf{Target}: 3-level classification (Graduate, Drop-out, Enrolled)
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Augmentation Methodology:} To enable multimodal analysis, we synthetically generated student comment data using GPT-4.5 (gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09 snapshot) through a structured prompting approach:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*,noitemsep]
    \item \textbf{Feature-guided generation}: For each student, we created 5 context-specific prompts incorporating their academic status, demographics, and performance metrics
    \begin{verbatim}
    "As a [age]-year-old [gender] [marital status] student with 
    [scholarship status] studying [course], who scored [grade] 
    in [course unit], write a forum post about [random academic topic]"
    \end{verbatim}

    \item \textbf{Academic realism}: Prompts incorporated domain-specific scenarios (assignment struggles, scheduling conflicts) validated by 3 subject matter experts

    \item \textbf{Diversity enforcement}: Generated comments spanned emotional tones (frustration, confusion, satisfaction) proportional to academic performance

    \item \textbf{Quality control}: 10\% of generated comments were manually verified against authenticity metrics (PAPA scale \cite{roberts2021synthetic})
\end{enumerate}

The resulting augmented dataset contains 22,115 synthetic comments (5 per student) stored in the \texttt{student\_comment} field. The complete augmented dataset and generation scripts are available in our project repository: \url{https://github.com/Milouden/TRIAD-Drop.git}.

