The remainder of the paper is organized as follows. Section 2 recalls the single player benchmark model with Epstein-Zin utility along with its game-theoretic extensions. Section \ref{sec:one-to-one} establishes a one-to-one correspondence between the Nash equilibrium and the solution to a certain BSDE. The sufficient condition—showing that a solution to the BSDE yields a Nash equilibrium—is presented in Section~\ref{sec:sufficient}. The necessary condition—showing that any Nash equilibrium must correspond to a BSDE solution—is developed in Section~\ref{sec:necessary}. 
