 In this section we establish our characterization of equilibrium result. We prove that any mean-field equilibrium satisfies a certain BSDE and that, conversely, any solution to the said BSDE yields a mean-field equilibrium. %Our 
 %analysis requires a necessary maximum principle for Epstein-Zin utility optimization problems. 
